 "version": "age_projection_v1_2026_11_22",
 "method": "Expected change from the builder's measured level to the next season's opening day, by age (LEBRON points). Evidence: Basketball Index separate-season LEBRON 2010-2026 (offense and defense), ages from Basketball Reference (development_evidence.json). For every player-season t with 1,000+ minutes: level = minutes-weighted blend of t, t-1, t-2 with the builder's season weights (1 / 0.7 / 0.45); lag = LEBRON in t+1 (500+ minutes) minus level; annual = LEBRON in t+1 minus LEBRON in t (the per-season change at that age). Opening day of t+1 = the t+1 season average minus half a season of change, so shift(age) = lag(age) - 0.5 x annual(age). The half season matters because the game's own monthly development runs through the season from opening day. Ages are the age in season t+1. Each side is smoothed across ages (Gaussian, 1.5 years). Survivors only: players who left the league are missing (13-22% of those 28 and older), so older players' decline is if anything understated.",
